  <Properties>
    <mediaPropertyAltText>
      <Value><![CDATA[The south front of Kedleston Hall, a Robert Adam Palladian mansion in honey-coloured stone with a central portico of six columns and matching pavilion wings, set behind a curved sweep of lawn.]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyAltText>
    <mediaPropertyCountry>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "United Kingdom"
]]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyCountry>
    <mediaPropertyDescription>
      <Value><![CDATA[Built between 1759 and 1765 for the Curzon family, Kedleston Hall boasts the most complete and least altered sequence of Robert Adam interiors in England and stands in a landscape park of formal pleasure grounds, lakes and rolling parkland.]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyDescription>
